    {
      "id": "bridge-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "**What data belongs to it?**\n\n```text\nbridge   { ref, role, resourceKind, scope, grants[] }\ntarget   { mode:'bridge', ref, kind, resourceKind, role, scope, grants[], key }\n_bridge  { sourceRef, entryPort, kind, targetKind, classKey, classRef }\n_classBinding { key, sourceRef }\n```\n\nThese four carry overlapping copies of the same facts — `data.bridge`, `data.target`, and top-level `data` fields all get written together, for legacy-compat reasons going back to earlier shapes. `components/GraphEditor/utils/bridgeSettings.js`'s `readBridgeSettings()`/`withBridge()` is the one place that knows how to read and write all three consistently — nothing else should hand-assemble a bridge patch.\n\nRequired at minimum: `role`, `resourceKind`, `ref`. For `resourceKind: node-class`, also the resolved `key`.\n\n`_bridge` and `_classBinding` describe provenance/binding on imported instances; they are not four interchangeable required fields on every Bridge node. Use readBridgeSettings/withBridge for the normalized Bridge data and bridgeEventSubscriptions for subscriptions. Bridge grants and subscriptions are different contracts.",
