    {
      "id": "bridge-representations",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Representations",
      "position": {
        "x": 380,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Representations",
        "body": "**How is it represented?**\n\nA Bridge typically renders as a small authority card naming its role, resourceKind, and target ref — never the target's own content. It points at what it grants; it doesn't inline it. A collapsed Bridge shows just enough to answer \"what does this graph have authority over, and in which direction,\" without requiring a fetch of the target to render at all.",
